<< {"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"cacheScope":"public","resultType":"complete","tools":[{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Start here if you are new to JETCARP. Explains what JETCARP is and how these tools fit together, with worked examples you can copy. `topic`: \"overview\" (default: concepts, coordinates, a glider in Life, Brian's Brain, a rule on hexagons, a sandpile), \"world\" (drawing, pasting, reseeding, commands, objects), \"library\" (finding, reading and curating patterns, ant runs and Quick Start entries), \"searches\" (long searches as background jobs: start, wait, read the finds, stop, resume), \"scripts\" (every run_script function), \"packs\" (checking, importing and publishing packs), \"setup\" (this installation as its user set it up: profile, folders, packs, GPU, library; read only, since setup is the user's choice) or \"pages\" (the pages of the JETCARP book). `page` returns one book page as Markdown, e.g. {\"page\": \"guides/searching\"} (the resources jetcarp://docs/{page}). `schema` returns the settings of a tool argument that names a jetcarp://schema/ resource, e.g. {\"schema\": \"search_start/hunt\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"page":{"description":"A page of the JETCARP book by its path without .md, e.g. \"guides/searching\" (topic pages lists them).","type":"string"},"schema":{"description":"A JSON Schema: a tool argument's settings (\"search_start/hunt\" is jetcarp://schema/search_start/hunt), \"scene.json\" or \"pack.json\".","type":"string"},"topic":{"description":"Which guide (default overview).","enum":["overview","world","library","searches","scripts","packs","setup","pages"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"help","title":"JETCARP help and worked examples"},{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Lists what there is to choose from. `what`: \"rules\" (default: the named rules with notation, family and a line each, and how rule notation works; any name or notation works as a CA's `rule`, e.g. \"Life\", \"B36/S23\", \"Brian's Brain\", \"W30\", \"Ant RL\"), \"tilings\" (tiling ids for world_new and their neighbour counts; with `search`, catalog tilings such as \"k2-005\" or \"3.4.6.4\"), \"isohedral\" (Kaplan's 81 isohedral tile types), \"palettes\" (built-in palettes and their colours), \"seeds\" (the forms a CA's `seed` takes), or \"commands\" (the command objects world_edit's `commands` applies). Examples: {\"what\": \"rules\", \"family\": \"Generations\"}, {\"what\": \"tilings\", \"search\": \"k2-\"}.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"family":{"description":"rules: only this family (part of its name, any case), e.g. \"Life-like\", \"Generations\", \"Agents\".","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"tilings: With `search`: most matches listed (default 60).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"search":{"description":"tilings: List the tilings (families, catalog tilings, isohedral types) whose id or name contains this text, any case, e.g. \"k2-\", \"3.4.6.4\", \"ih4\". Default: the tiling families.","type":"string"},"what":{"description":"What to list (default rules).","enum":["rules","tilings","isohedral","palettes","seeds","commands"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"reference","title":"Rules, tilings, palettes, seeds, commands"},{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"openWorldHint":false},"description":"Replaces the current world. Build one from a tiling (the grid of cells) and the CAs (cellular automata) that run on it: {\"tiling\": \"hex\", \"width\": 60, \"height\": 60, \"boundary\": \"wrap\", \"cas\": [\"B24/S35\"]}. Each CA starts from its rule's default seed (a random soup for Life-like rules) unless given one: {\"cas\": [{\"rule\": \"Life\", \"seed\": \"empty\"}]} is a blank field to draw on (reference {\"what\": \"seeds\"} lists the seeds, {\"what\": \"tilings\"} the tilings). Size: width and height (8 to 4096 unit cells each), or `cells` (about that many, up to 4000000), or `level` on aperiodic tilings. Or open one: `quickstart` (a Quick Start entry by handle, e.g. \"life\"), `pattern` (a library pattern on a grid sized for it, e.g. \"glider\"), `scene` (scene JSON, as world_status {\"scene\": true} returns it) or `path` (a scene file). Returns the world's status with each CA's id. Next: world_edit, world_step, world_read, world_render.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"boundary":{"description":"\"wrap\" (default), \"dead\", or \"live\" (aperiodic tilings are always dead).","type":"string"},"cas":{"description":"The CAs, in order: rule names or notation (\"Life\", \"B3/S23\"), or CA objects as in a scene ({\"rule\": \"Life\", \"seed\": \"random:0.2\"}); one string is one CA."},"cells":{"description":"Instead of width and height: about this many cells in a roughly square region.","type":"integer"},"height":{"description":"Grid height in unit cells.","type":"integer"},"level":{"description":"Aperiodic tilings: the substitution level.","type":"integer"},"name":{"description":"Scene name.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"A scene .json file.","type":"string"},"pattern":{"description":"A library pattern (id, prefix or name, e.g. `glider`) alone on a wrapped grid sized for it, in a rule it runs in.","type":"string"},"quickstart":{"description":"A Quick Start entry by handle (`life`, `find:<id>`, `atlas:<...>`, `qs-<hex>`): the scene the app's Quick Start opens.","type":"string"},"rng_seed":{"description":"Random seed (default 1): the same seed gives the same run. Any `u64`; beyond 2^53 - 1 also as a string of decimal digits.","minimum":0,"pattern":"^[0-9]+$","type":["integer","string"]},"scene":{"description":"Scene JSON: the object, or its text."},"tiling":{"description":"Tiling id (reference {\"what\": \"tilings\"}): \"square\" (default), \"hex\", \"triangle\", \"cairo\", \"spectre\" (aperiodic), a vertex configuration such as \"3.4.6.4\", or a catalog id such as \"k